<title>SINGAPORE: Vietnam Dai Hung cargo awarded to S.Korean refiner.</title>
<headline>Vietnam Dai Hung cargo awarded to S.Korean refiner.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The consortium operating the Vietnamese Dai Hung crude field has awarded its latest sell tender to a South Korean refiner at Minas APPI +43 cents per barrel, sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The consortium offered the 450,000-barrel cargo of Dai Hung crude loading between end June and early July in a tender which closed May 28.</p>
<p>In the last sell tender, a June cargo was awarded to Japan's Sumitomo at Minas APPI +20/30.  </p>
<p>The equity producers of the Dai Hung field are Malaysia's state-owned Petronas, with 20 percent, Japan's Sumitomo with 10.625 percent, France's Total SA with 10.625 percent and state-owned Petrovietnam, with 15 percent.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3081)</p>
